  "name": "WeatherTech Raceway Laguna Seca",
  "notes": {
    "overview": "Laguna Seca is a short, brutally undulating 3.6 km circuit with over 90 m of elevation change, mixing slow hairpins with fast, blind, downhill corners. Rhythm and commitment matter more than outright grip. The signature is the Corkscrew (T8-T9), a blind plunging left-right drop. Nail the exits of the two hairpins (Andretti and the final left) for lap time, since both feed long straights.",
    "corners": {
      "1": "Downhill entry off the front straight into the hairpin braking zone. Brake in a straight line before turning in; the surface falls away, so early trail-braking upsets the car. Sets up the Andretti apex.",
      "2": "The Andretti Hairpin. Long, downhill left; brake earlier than it looks because it drops away. Take a late apex around the second set of inside kerbs, then feed throttle progressively toward the climb.",
      "3": "Quick right as the track begins to climb. Short braking, rotate the car early so you can commit to throttle up the hill and carry momentum toward Turn 4.",
      "4": "Uphill right; keep the car settled on the climb. A clean, early apex lets you get power down for the run up to the mid-lap left-handers.",
      "5": "Left as the track keeps rising. Momentum corner; protect entry speed and let the gradient scrub pace rather than over-braking, then flow toward Turn 6.",
      "6": "Left near the top of the hill. Keep it tidy and positioned for the fast run up to the Corkscrew; don't waste speed you carry onto the climb.",
      "7": "Fast right on the run toward the Corkscrew. Stay committed, settle the car and get positioned left, because this sets your entry line into the drop that follows.",
      "8": "Corkscrew entry: blind, plunging left over the crest. Aim at your marker and commit, you can't see the exit. Turn in as the nose drops and the track falls away.",
      "9": "Corkscrew exit: immediate right as the track plummets. Let the car fall down the hill, unwind the wheel and get throttle down early for the run to Rainey Curve.",
      "10": "Rainey Curve: long, downhill left taken at speed after the Corkscrew drop. Be patient on entry; camber and gradient help, but running wide costs you all the way down toward the final complex.",
      "11": "Downhill right leading toward the final hairpin. Short braking, rotate and settle the car so a tidy exit lines you up for the last corner.",
      "12": "The final hairpin, a slow left onto the main straight. Brake deep, sacrifice entry for a clean early throttle exit; this drive sets your speed down the whole front straight."
    },
